# 20. Useful Commands

### List CRDs

```bash
kubectl get crd
```

### Get a specific CRD

```bash
kubectl get crd myapplications.apps.example.com
```

### Describe CRD

```bash
kubectl describe crd myapplications.apps.example.com
```

### Get CRD YAML

```bash
kubectl get crd myapplications.apps.example.com -o yaml
```

### List Custom Resources

```bash
kubectl get myapplications
```

### Get all resources of a custom type

```bash
kubectl get myapplications -A
```

### Describe Custom Resource

```bash
kubectl describe myapplication chat-app
```

### Delete Custom Resource

```bash
kubectl delete myapplication chat-app
```

### Delete CRD

```bash
kubectl delete crd myapplications.apps.example.com
```

Deleting a CRD should be done carefully because it also affects the custom resources associated with that definition.

